      <abstract>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;A lightning talk about OSSIE, a Software Defined Radios(SDR) implementation.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA; </abstract>
      <description>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The talk will introduce software defined&#xA;radio and talk about several open source SDR projects. The talk will focus on&#xA;explaining what SDR is, why the open source developer would be interested&#xA;in it, and ways to get started. &#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;i&gt;About OSSIE:&lt;/i&gt;&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;OSSIE is an implementation of the Software Communication Architecture(SCA).&#xA;The SCA provides a structure for implementing Software Defined Radios&#xA;(SDR) using a component based architecture. OSSIE currently runs on&#xA;regular PC&amp;#39;s and a TI OMAP Starter Kit (OSK). OSSIE runs primarily on&#xA;Linux based machines (although other Unix&amp;#39;s should work OK).&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA; </description>
